            <p class="Q1List">1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Benson method of toughness and tenacity: Scott tester, inch-pounds @ 77&deg;F, 20 inches per minute pull. Tension head 7/8&quot; diameter.</p>

            <p class="Q1List">2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon standing undisturbed for a period of 24 hours, the emulsion shall show no white milky film upon the surface.</p>

            <p class="Q1List">3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The base asphalt shall be modified prior to emulsification.</p>

            <p class="Q1List">4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The emulsion shall be precertified prior to use. A one-quart sample each of the base asphalt and polymer shall be supplied to the agency 10 days in advance to the project start.</p>

            <p class="HistoryNote">(Ord. 2017-22, Rep&amp;ReEn, 07/05/2017)</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="13.21.001.0716.2.1"><a name="13.21.001.0716.2.1">13-21-001-0716.2.1</a> MAG Spec 716.2.1 &ndash; Cover Material &ndash; Stone Chips &ndash; General</h3>
            <p class="P0">First paragraph, revise to include the following:</p>

            <p class="Q1">No volcanic cinders will be acceptable for cover material.</p>

            <p class="HistoryNote">(Ord. 2017-22, Rep&amp;ReEn, 07/05/2017)</p>

